  "response": "The exact characterization, proof, and worked examples have been verified with `opus` and `sol` and finalized in `/work/answer.md`, with `[argon] FINAL` recorded on `/work/board.md`.\n\nFor positive values ($v_A, v_B, v_C, v_P > 0$ with $d := v_A + v_B + v_C - v_P > 0$), the Vickrey-nearest core point equals the centroid of $F$ **if and only if** at least one of the following holds:\n1. $v_P \\le \\min(v_A, v_B, v_C)$,\n2. $d \\le \\min(v_A, v_B, v_C)$, or\n3. $v_A = v_B = v_C$ (and always in the lower-dimensional degenerate cases $v_P = 0$ or $\\min(v_A, v_B, v_C) = 0$).",
